<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῐθόλογ-ος</span></b> , ὁ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγω</span> (B) <i><span class="en">
			1
		</span></i>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who picks out
				stones for building</i>: hence, <i>one who builds with stones
				picked out</i> to fit their places, not squared (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λογάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>BSA</u>
				3.112
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Athens</span>): so generally,
			<i>mason</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				858b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθολόγοι καὶ τέκτονες</span>
			<i>masons</i> and joiners, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.44
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.4.18
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
